# Top-level safety net for the monorepo.
#
# Each rig keeps its own .gitignore with rig-specific rules (private docs, benchmark
# runs held back from publication). This file covers the patterns that must never be
# committed from ANY rig, so a rig whose own .gitignore misses one is still protected.
#
# Note: `tpu.env` is deliberately NOT ignored — it is a rig's committed source of
# truth for deployment parameters. Do not add `*.env` here, it would match it.

# Secrets and machine-local config
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
credentials*.json
service-account*.json

# Generated MCP registration — embeds the GCP project id, regenerate with project-setup.sh
.mcp.json

# Machine-specific Claude Code settings (.claude/settings.json IS committed and shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Private, not-for-publication docs
tpu.md
pytorch.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.Python
env/
venv/
.venv/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
.cache
coverage.xml
*.cover
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Model weights and other large artifacts
gemma-4-*/
gemma-*/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.tar.gz
*.pth
*.onnx

# Editor and OS noise.
#
# Deliberately NO blanket `*.log` rule here: benchmark runs under benchmarks/runs/**
# commit their logs as the record of a measurement. tpu-vllm-v5e1-2b ignores `*.log`
# in its own .gitignore, which is the right scope for it.
*.swp
*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
